# Shell scripts must be LF whatever the machine they were last edited on: a `.sh` checked out
# with CRLF fails on Linux with `$'\r': command not found`, which is a confusing way for a release
# to break. This repository is worked on from Windows, where `core.autocrlf` would otherwise
# decide.
*.sh text eol=lf

# The guide, whose reference pages are written by a test: LF so a Windows checkout and a
# Linux CI run produce byte-identical files and the pages never churn.
docs/guide/** text eol=lf

# ...but not the pictures. `text` on a PNG rewrites any byte pair that happens to look like a
# line ending and quietly corrupts it: a 20,677-byte render of a dovetail went into git as
# 20,676 and came back out broken. `binary` is what the rule above must never reach.
docs/guide/**/*.png binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
